# Copy to `.env.development` or `.env.local` as needed (Vite loads .env.* automatically).

# Point REST + WebSocket at the Go server so they do not share the browser's per-host
# connection limit with Vite (6688). See vite.config.ts header comment.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7633
#
# If you use the default (empty) base URL, Vite proxies /api and /ws to VITE_DEV_API_ORIGIN
# (default http://127.0.0.1:7633). ECONNREFUSED / ws EPIPE in the terminal means the Go
# server was not listening yet or restarted — start `go run ./cmd/server` first.

# Optional explicit WS base (otherwise derived from VITE_API_BASE_URL or page host).
# VITE_WS_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:7633/ws
